      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the teardown ordering is inverted. handle_lpi_disable unshares and unpins the property and pending tables before GICR_CTLR is written, so even in the good case there is a window where the pages are host owned again while the redistributor is still enabled against them. enable_lpi has it the right way round, tables first and then the register.\n\nCould the write and the release swap places here?",
